1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,474
Fourteen monitors turned red at once.

2
00:00:03,514 --> 00:00:08,247
"NATO's out, sir. Japan
too. Korea. Australia."

3
00:00:08,287 --> 00:00:13,804
An alliance is a system, and systems
always flow toward their own interests.

4
00:00:13,844 --> 00:00:17,400
A war you start alone, you finish alone.

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:23,352
The cable from the U.S. Embassy was two
lines long. Join the Hormuz operation.

6
00:00:23,392 --> 00:00:26,401
The reply had already
gone out under his name.

7
00:00:26,441 --> 00:00:30,338
"We support it, but we won't
take part. That's all."

8
00:00:30,378 --> 00:00:34,535
Refusals always arrive in a
properly formatted document.

9
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:38,998
The children were asleep.
Then the ceiling shook.

10
00:00:39,038 --> 00:00:42,282
Her five-year-old cried,
not even sure why.

11
00:00:42,322 --> 00:00:46,271
Smoke rose from the building
next door. There were no lights.

12
00:00:46,311 --> 00:00:52,558
In the darkness a war leaves behind, the
ones who cry are always the children.

13
00:00:52,758 --> 00:00:56,368
The pilot checked the
coordinates. Then checked again.

14
00:00:56,408 --> 00:01:03,466
The release button takes two fingers.
One is a mistake. Two is a decision.

15
00:01:03,506 --> 00:01:08,370
At 5:12 AM, Iranian state TV
confirmed Larijani's death.

16
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:13,116
The oldest channel in Iran's
nuclear diplomacy had closed.

17
00:01:13,316 --> 00:01:17,030
The retaliation came one hour
and forty-two minutes later.

18
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:21,620
David Levy, seventy-two, did
not go down to the shelter.

19
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:26,759
Not because I didn't take shelter.
Because the war came looking for me.

20
00:01:26,799 --> 00:01:32,262
Civilians never choose war.
War always chooses civilians.

21
00:01:32,462 --> 00:01:35,523
The Merkava tanks were ominously quiet.

22
00:01:35,563 --> 00:01:39,591
This was not an air strike.
It came across the ground.

23
00:01:39,631 --> 00:01:41,726
A border is a line on a map.

24
00:01:41,766 --> 00:01:45,923
Tank treads roll over it,
and the line is erased.

25
00:01:46,123 --> 00:01:49,785
Children killed or
wounded: more than 1,100.

26
00:01:49,825 --> 00:01:52,991
The report had no names. Numbers are tidy.

27
00:01:53,031 --> 00:01:58,076
Children don't know why anyone is
fighting. Adults think they do.

28
00:01:58,276 --> 00:02:02,042
A reed only sings once it has
been torn from the reed bed.

29
00:02:02,082 --> 00:02:06,319
Whether it's a melody or a scream
depends on the ear that hears it.

30
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:09,943
The cruelest moment of war
is when we get used to it.

31
00:02:09,983 --> 00:02:12,390
Continued in Episode 7.
